description.narrative:
Truck traffic across the border increased from 100 trucks per day in 2009 to 220 trucks per day by December 2018 Progress/Status: VIE Component: Truck traffic across the border decreased from 100 trucks per day in 2009 to 29 trucks per day as end of 2018;
LAO Component: Truck traffic across the border increased from under 100 trucks per day in 2009 to 250 trucks per day in June 2020.
The benefit monitoring and evaluation (BME) report shows that the number of truck traffic across the borders increased significantly after road had been improved. Analysis show that, the peak day in 2020, there were truck traffic up to 317 trucks across the borders. Data Source: MOT and MPWT traffic statistics BME report submitted by PMU TL in May 2019 Actual value:
